        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:04 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court Record",
      "case_id": "2008-07-689",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "e69bf5be13291cabe5482902a0a58e4295531c68b41562a19cc50a48479e27bb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e69bf5be1329-0000-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES: CHRISTOPHER G. BROWNING, JR., ESQ., Solicitor General, Raleigh, N.C.; on behalf of the Petitioners. CARL W. THURMAN, III, ESQ., Wilmington, N.C.; on behalf of the Respondents. DARYL JOSEFFER, ESQ., Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting the Respondents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Christopher G. Browning, Jr., Esq. (Petitioners)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-689",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "e69bf5be13291cabe5482902a0a58e4295531c68b41562a19cc50a48479e27bb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e69bf5be1329-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Voting Rights Act should be interpreted in such a way as to encourage a transition to a society where race no longer matters. In North Carolina, coalition districts have been crucial in moving towards Congress's ultimate goal. Coalition districts bring races together by fostering political alliances across racial lines. As a result they serve to diminish racial polarization over time. Coalition districts help us in reaching the point where race will no longer matter in drawing district lines. These districts bring us one step closer to fulfilling our Nation's moral and ethical obligation to create an integrated society."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-07-689",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "e69bf5be13291cabe5482902a0a58e4295531c68b41562a19cc50a48479e27bb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e69bf5be1329-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: But under your definition of coalition district, race is the key factor."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Christopher G. Browning, Jr., Esq.",
      "case_id": "2008-07-689",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "e69bf5be13291cabe5482902a0a58e4295531c68b41562a19cc50a48479e27bb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e69bf5be1329-0000-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BROWNING: Your Honor, the decision in LULAC makes clear that influence districts are not protected under section 2 of the Voting Rights Act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-07-689",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "e69bf5be13291cabe5482902a0a58e4295531c68b41562a19cc50a48479e27bb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e69bf5be1329-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: If that's the case, then your test imposes a statistical standard just as your opponent's test does, doesn't it? It's just a different one."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Christopher G. Browning, Jr., Esq. (Petitioners)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-689",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "e69bf5be13291cabe5482902a0a58e4295531c68b41562a19cc50a48479e27bb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e69bf5be1329-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BROWNING: Yes, Your Honor. What we're proposing and what we think is required by the text of section 2 is you simply take the existing Gingles factors and you look at the amount of racially polarized voting, and from that you are able to readily calculate the size of the minority group that would be sufficiently large to elect a minority -- a minority candidate."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-07-689",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e69bf5be13291cabe5482902a0a58e4295531c68b41562a19cc50a48479e27bb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e69bf5be1329-0001-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the district that you want to draw, the crossover district, would have 39 percent African-American voters. The district that complied with State law of the county line would have 35 percent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2008-07-689",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e69bf5be13291cabe5482902a0a58e4295531c68b41562a19cc50a48479e27bb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e69bf5be1329-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The rule proposed by Petitioners in this case would effectively require maximization resulting in, as the Court has recognized, judicial involvement in many, many more situations."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-689",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e69bf5be13291cabe5482902a0a58e4295531c68b41562a19cc50a48479e27bb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e69bf5be1329-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't know why it would require maximization."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-689",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e69bf5be13291cabe5482902a0a58e4295531c68b41562a19cc50a48479e27bb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e69bf5be1329-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: But -- but you are saying it's an opportunity, and what you mean is it is sufficient to provide an opportunity. And Justice Breyer's question is: Isn't the two-to-one ratio something that we should consider as also being sufficient to provide an opportunity?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners (Christopher G. Browning)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-689",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e69bf5be13291cabe5482902a0a58e4295531c68b41562a19cc50a48479e27bb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e69bf5be1329-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "REBUTTAL ARGUMENT OF CHRISTOPHER G. BROWNING ON BEHALF OF THE PETITIONERS MR. BROWNING: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice. Let me start first of all with Justice Breyer's question about the arbitrary nature of the 50 percent rule. The 50 percent rule, let there be no doubt, is extremely arbitrary, even under the government's 2 percent cushion."
    },
